  "id": "confusable-writes-local",
  "title": "setConfusable and the confusable lists are answered on the device (C-31, rule L-10)",
  "covers": [
    "confusables.writes_local"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Two kana-only words. Before C-31 the shell forwarded setConfusable and (first draft of C-31) cached the lists; with the write local the lists are local too, so the pair shows at once.",
    "Step 0: no pair yet.",
    "Steps 1-3: setConfusable creates the pair as confirmed (a hand-made pair is simply a confirmed one); both lists show it.",
    "Steps 4-6: rejecting it is a register write on the same row; the status filter follows.",
    "Step 7: the same note twice is 422. Step 8: a note that does not exist is 404.",
    "No worker runs in either harness, so no confusable.suggested op exists."
  ],
